Oracle8i, Oracle Internet Application Server 8i (Oracle iAS), and the Oracle
Internet Developer Suite, across Compaq server platforms will enable
customers of all sizes to implement comprehensive e-business solutions with
flexibility, efficiency, and deployment ease. Such cross-platform
integration will allow customers to write Java* applications once and deploy
them across all Compaq platforms. Additionally, the scalability of Compaq's
servers and the Oracle Internet Platform software offer customers the widest
possible range of deployment options--from a single server to a large
cluster, allowing them to grow their infrastructure while maintaining their
technology investments. 

	"This agreement between Oracle and Compaq represents a new level of
commitment to provide an exceptionally reliable, scalable and complete
e-business infrastructure to the widest range of customers possible," said
Gary Bloom, executive vice president, Oracle. "The breadth of Compaq's
server platforms and storage offerings, coupled with the power of the
complete Oracle Internet Platform, will provide our customers with an
unbeatable infrastructure for developing and deploying e-business
solutions." 

