In article <395C3589.BAB2FE30@home.com>, DC <dcinca2000@home.com> wrote:

>And the other 6 comets are still worth keeping?? Fine hardware!

Comet was indeed fine hardware. It was, however, a VAX-11/750.

The VAX-11/730 was Nebula and the VAX-11/725 (a lower cost, bounded variant) 
was Low Cost Nebula (usually just LCN).

To answer the original question the DAP module on the KA730 is the M8390.
It would be the Data Path module of the CPU.
The memory controller would be M8391 and the WCS (writeable control store for 
the microcode) would be M8394.

Good luck fixing it :-)

Antonio

