drivera@inktomi.com wrote:
: Does anyone know which file to modify that will allow me to configure
: my 10/100 ethernet car for full-duplex 100?

You can achieve this in several places. One place is SRM ew?0_mode
variables. Setting it to FastFD will do that you want. Another place
is in /etc/rc.config: Adding "speed 200" to the appropriate IFCONFIG_? 
variable will do the trick. The rc.config's setting will override 
any SRM value. There are other, more obscure ways to achieve the same
effect, too.

Which one of those is the "correct" place is really up to your system
administration policies.

Incidentally, the information you were looking for is readily available
from Tru64 network management guide (available online). The ifconfig
manual page, which should be installed on your system, also contains
sufficient information for you to be able to deduce the rc.config
technique.

/Serge.P

