Questions for you...

Venturis DUAL ???  I don't think DEC ever made a dual 486 Venturis.

Whether or not the computer works with the Creative 24x CD-ROM depends
VERY much on the BIOS.  Many older 486s simply fail to boot up when an
EIDE/ATAPI CD-ROM drive is cabled in.  Others do not "recognize" and
identify a CD-ROM drive in the BIOS, but the drive works anyway
because there is a supporting driver(s) in CONFIG.SYS and MSCDEX.EXE
is run within AUTOEXEC.BAT.

Try www.windrivers.com for drivers if your Creative 24x did not come
with drivers.  Look for the Oak Technology driver, a universal
EIDE/ATAPI CD-ROM driver, simple to use because it autodetects the
drives without need for command line switches... Ben Myers

