Got a customer who wanted to upgrade a HSJ40 (dual redundant mode)
to a HSJ50. He asked if it were possible to failover one of the HSJ40s and
replace it with a HSJ50. Then copy the configuration from the hsj40 to the
hsj50. Then boot the HSJ50 by failing the remaining HSJ40. THEN replacing
the
HSJ40 with the last HSJ50 module. Copy the config files and the set the
controllers to dual redundant mode. My first answer was no because of the
possible microcode mismatch errors. WELL, they tried it on a test bed and
it WORKED!! Go figure.

Regards,

Bob Scarborough





