In article <8i8gmg$t98$1@uni00nw.unity.ncsu.edu>,
  BSD Bob <bobkey@weedcon1.cropsci.ncsu.edu> wrote:
> I was trying to hook up a headless VS3100/M38 to a vt330 terminal
using
> supposedly MMJ cables (I went by a local cable shop to get a straight
> and a null made up).  Alas, they don't seem to work.  Can anyone point
> me to the pinouts for a standard DEC MMJ cable?

From the OpenVMS FAQ found via http://eisner.decus.org/vms/faq.htm :-

MISC1.  Looking for connector wiring pinouts?

DECconnect DEC-423 MMJ pinout:

  1: Data Terminal Ready (DTR)
  2: Transmit (TXD)
  3: Transmit Ground (TXD-)
  4: Receive Ground (RXD-)
  5: Receive (RXD)
  6: Data Set Ready (DSR)

   +------------------+
   | 1  2  3  4  5  6 |
   +------------+    ++
                +____+

If you hold your cable with the two ends facing one another and both
tabs facing you, then the wires that meet each other should have the
same colours.

> The monitor is fine,
> unless I have the proms set incorrectly to use the mmj i/o rather than
> the db25 i/o.

Go to Setup (F3)\Global Set-up\Comm1 Port and ensure it says DEC-423.
Press a left or right arrow key to change it not. Use Communications
setup to set speed, data bits, parity etc. (I'm assuming the setup
screens on VT330 and VT340 are the same.)

>  The VAX is fine on a vt420 with a real DEC MMJ cable.

I'm not clear from this whether you've tried the VT330 with the real
DEC cable and/or the VT420 with your made up cable. Sadly, it's not
unknown for everything on a VT to work except the serial comms which
blows up all too easily -- I've got several VT340s like this, and if
anyone can point me to the I/O chips on the main board, I may be able
to fix 'em.

Chris


