In article <8i8gmg$t98$1@uni00nw.unity.ncsu.edu>, BSD Bob <bobkey@weedcon1.cropsci.ncsu.edu> wrote:
>I was trying to hook up a headless VS3100/M38 to a vt330 terminal using
>supposedly MMJ cables (I went by a local cable shop to get a straight
>and a null made up).  Alas, they don't seem to work.  Can anyone point

I don't know what you mean by "null". The cable is either straight-through 
(1-1, 2-2, 3-3 etc.) or "flipped"  (1-6, 2-5, 3-4 etc.). So hold the two ends 
one in each hand same way up and either the colours match up exactly 
left-right and lef-right or they match as you read each one "outside" to 
"inside".

>me to the pinouts for a standard DEC MMJ cable?  The monitor is fine,
>unless I have the proms set incorrectly to use the mmj i/o rather than
>the db25 i/o.  The VAX is fine on a vt420 with a real DEC MMJ cable.

VT420 and VT320 are the same so far as MMJ connection goes.
Given that you have a working setup you can:

a) look at the working cable and determine whether it is straigh-through or 
flipped, then decide if the one you have is right or wrong.

b) Start with the working setup and swap the VT420 for the VT330. Now you know 
whether the VT330 is OK or misconfigured.

c) Start with the working setup and swap in whichever of your two cables looks 
like it is wired appropriately. Now you know whether the cable is OK or not. 
(I've made a few of these up in the past and it is *easy* to make a cable that 
looks right but simply does not work because the crimp didn't quite work).

d) Now at least you either know that one or more of your cable and your VT330 
is broken, OR you plug in the VT330 using your cable and it will all work.

BTW- you have this working already so there is no need to go through the "flip 
switch 3" and "make sure you are plugged into the printer prot for alternate 
console" stuff. But just so noone gets the wrong idea, the VAX consoles are 
not like Alpha consoles. You do NOT do a "set console serial" to enable a 
serial port console. You just get to flip a switch.

