The Network Access Software CD V2.3a which comes with recently purchased
DS700's (now from
Cabletron) has many documents.

But the Digital/Compaq Web site also has these; start at:
http://www.service.digital.com/netrider/index.html


You can load the software from Ultrix (using MOP or Bootp), from Digital
Unix (bootp)
and probably from any other bootp implementation.

"Andy.Jack@nottingham.ac.uk" wrote:
> 
> We have a number of DECservers that have come out of service, including
> some DS700s which I believe could still be useful. As the time is
