Is there a list somewhere of what (if anything) may be used with an
industrial process control software package in "restricted" countries?

I've spent a long time surfing Compaq and US/UK government sites and
elsewhere, but can't find a list of specifics.

Rumour has it we can't use Alphas, DECnet, or NT systems. We might sell
a legacy VAX/VMS based product, but we need multiple serial ports. At
one time the DECserver VMSINSTAL used to say "you can't be in a
restricted country", but it no longer does. Doea this mean we can use
it now? If not, a 3100 with "harmonica" is OK, but long term
supply/support of this kit could be a problem.

I'm told we aren't allowed to export any hardware, but customers seem
to be able to source it locally. How they get it, I find it best not to
ask :-).

Can anyone get me out of the clouds of rumour into some solid info, or
possibly suggest a better NG to ask on? (Sorry if it's OT here, but
here is one of the places I lurk.)

TIA

Chris


