On Tue, 06 Jun 2000 19:01:19 GMT, "firewind" <auspoly@hotmail.com>
wrote:

>I have a Digital HiNote VP 525 120Mhz and need to remove the hard disk but
>can't work out how to get the case apart.
>Any help gratefully received. This is driving me mad!!!

I think this is simple, and doesn't involve taking the case apart.

As the notebook is facing you (as you would use it), you will see on
the left front edge a "panel" which slides to the left.  It is held in
place by a Philips screw on the underside of the unit.  Remove the
screw, then slide the panel off to the left - you may have to push in
on it a bit to get it to move.  The hard disk is in a carrier with a
wire handle that swings up - just pull on the handle.

The disk is a standard notebook IDE disk, but I think 2.1GB is the max
you can use.  If you buy the disk separately, you can carefully remove
the old one from the carrier and its connector and insert the new one
(I've done this), then just slide the carrier back in place, fold down
the handle and replace the cover panel.



