Dear Customer,

Thank you for your interest in the OpenVMS Version 7.3 Software Developer
Kit (SDK) Program.   We feel that this program has been very successful in 
the past, and we hope that you will decide to participate.

The OpenVMS Version 7.3-EFT1 SDK will be available in July 2000 as an
orderable kit through our DECdirect channel.  You can order the kit by 
ordering part number QA-MT3AD-H8 at a cost of $39.95.   Once the kit is 
available, it will be as simple as calling 1-800-ATCOMPAQ.  Business 
Partners can order it on the Web through the Compaq Business Link at
www.businesslink.compaq.com.

The V7.3-EFT1 SDK will contain early releases of the OpenVMS V7.3 VAX and
Alpha operating systems, as well as DECwindows and network products.  The 
SDK will also contain many new features including:

o Write Bitmap and Shadow Minicopy -- Performance and availability
  enhancements to Shadowing full copy.

o Switched LAN as a cluster interconnect:

  - Support for Gigabit Ethernet and ATM as full switched cluster
    interconnects.

  - Allows all LAN devices to participate in load distribution of 
    cluster traffic.

o Lock Manager 2000 (Alpha only) -- Enhancements that improve cluster 
  and application performance, SMP system performance, and scalability 
  and application availability.

o Extended File Cache (XFC) Version 1.0 support (Alpha only) -- Replacement
  for VIOC.  Extends the capabilities of cluster file cache.

o RMS Locking -- Reduces global buffer bucket locks by removing locks for
  read operations.  Also allows RMS to read a record without taking a 
  record lock.

o Kerberos Version 5 Security Client (Alpha only) -- Allows OpenVMS
  applications to communicate and authenticate with NT5 domains and 
  most UNIX platforms.

o Clusterwide Intrusion Detection -- Expands the current individual
  node-base intrusion detection in OpenVMS today to be cluster-wide 
  and cluster aware.

o QIO Server (Alpha only) -- Provides improved performance over MSCP,
  improved scaling and system management control, reduced maintenance 
  cost, and a public device driver interface to support third party 
  driver writers.

o SCSI Fastpath (Alpha only) -- Improves SCSI performance and scaling 
  in SMP systems.

o And more.  


The OpenVMS Version 7.3-EFT2 SDK is presently scheduled to be available in
September/October  2000.  Customers can choose to either purchase both the 
OpenVMS Version 7.3-EFT1 SDK and the OpenVMS Version 7.3-EFT2 SDK at a cost 
of $39.95 each, or just select one.

Support for the SDK program will continue to be through the following
Internet newsgroup:

      vmsnet.sdk.openvms.fieldtest

Please see the OpenVMS Web Page www.openvms.compaq.com  in late June 2000
timeframe for additional information for ordering this kit.

Your involvement and support have been very important to the success of the
overall SDK Program.  We hope that you will continue to support Version 
7.3-EFT1 as this program moves forward.

Sincerely,

OpenVMS Product Management




