Linux supports many PCI cards that work under X/i386 also under X/Alpha.
NetBSD only supports the ZLXp-E1 under X. Don't know about FreeBSD.

IIRC the "Mach64" was supported under DU4.0c, so this should still be
the case with True64. While "Mach64" is a very generic description, you
may want to find a used no-frills ATI Mach64 and try it. Should be in
the USD 25,- price range today.

