>limitations in the underlying system.

I don't think that's the case.  Certainly, the machine has more than 
enough memory bandwidth to handle a decent PCI graphics accellerator
at 1024x768x32.  For 3D applications without a *lot* of on-card
RAM and good drivers, I would agree that the box (or, most probably,
its PCI and memory buses) can't hack it.

But 8MB TGA and TGA2 cards are out there at decent prices, and will
provide solid X11 performance for 2D applications, without requiring
much change to the system beyond dropping in the new card.

