On Wed, 14 Jun 2000 17:39:47 +0200, JeP <JP.Dzisiak@ulg.ac.be> wrote:

>Hello !
>
>I have compiled some programs on a DEC-UNIX 4.0D with the DEC FORTRAN
>and I like to run them on another DEC workstation. However this target
>workstation has no compiler nor run-time. My question is: is it possible
>to install the FORTRAN run-time on this workstation WITHOUT any licence.
>I mean extract the run-time codes from the "Software Product Library"
>CDROMS without any key...

The Fortran run-time library is in a separate subset called DFARTLnnn
on the product CD.  Yes, you can install that on any DIGITAL UNIX
system without a compiler license.


